      "role": "user",
      "content": "Sometimes I sit in my study and I just look at the stacks of books I spent forty years compiling, all these monographs and papers... and it feels like I'm looking at a graveyard. Everything I thought was foundational has been digitized, parsed, and rendered obsolete by algorithms in a matter of months. It's like I've spent my whole life building a cathedral only to wake up and find out the world has moved on to living in tents. I feel like a ghost in my own life.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
